<% content_for :title, "Files" %>

<div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 mb-8 items-start">
  <section class="min-w-0">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-2">Run a file</h1>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-3">
      Each file's page runs it with the same command you type in the terminal and shows what it
      printed. Change the file, save it, and refresh the page to run it again.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 mb-2">
      Only the files that came with this repo are listed. A file you add yourself still runs in the
      terminal, but it won't appear here: listing it takes new code in the app itself, which you'll
      see how to write when you build web pages of your own.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-stone-600">
      <code>code-along-complete/</code> isn't listed either. It's there to catch up from: copy what you
      need into your own file in <code>code-along/</code> and run that, here or in the terminal.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="min-w-0 bg-white border border-stone-200 rounded p-4">
    <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-stone-600 mb-2">In the terminal</h2>
    <p class="text-stone-700 mb-2">
      The server keeps its terminal busy, so open a second one with the <strong>+</strong> on the
      terminal panel. From the top folder of the repo (where README.md is), run:
    </p>
    <code class="block bg-stone-900 text-stone-100 px-3 py-2 rounded text-sm mb-2">bin/rails runner code-along/1-data.rb</code>
    <p class="text-sm text-stone-600">
      Change the path to run a different file. Every file's page shows its exact command.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>

<div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
  <% @folders.each do |folder, files| %>
    <section>
      <h2 class="font-mono font-semibold"><%= folder %>/</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 mb-2"><%= RubyFile::FOLDERS[folder] %></p>
      <ul class="border-t border-stone-200">
        <% files.each do |file| %>
          <li class="border-b border-stone-200">
            <%= link_to file.name, ruby_file_path(file.path), class: "block py-1.5 font-mono text-sm hover:bg-stone-100" %>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    </section>
  <% end %>
</div>
